## 🚀 Despliegue

### Backend (Node.js + Express)

#### 1. Preparar Servidor

```bash
# Instalar Node.js y PM2
curl -fsSL https://deb.nodesource.com/setup_18.x | sudo -E bash -
sudo apt-get install -y nodejs
sudo npm install -g pm2
```

#### 2. Configurar Aplicación

```bash
# Clonar repositorio
git clone https://github.com/tu-repo/ionik-backend.git
cd ionik-backend

# Instalar dependencias
npm install

# Configurar variables de entorno
cp .env.example .env
nano .env

# Iniciar con PM2
pm2 start server.js --name ionik-api
pm2 save
pm2 startup
```

#### 3. Configurar Nginx

```nginx
# /etc/nginx/sites-available/ionik-api
server {
    listen 80;
    server_name api.ionik.com;
    
    location / {
        proxy_pass http://localhost:3000;
        proxy_http_version 1.1;
        proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;
        proxy_set_header Connection 'upgrade';
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        proxy_cache_bypass $http_upgrade;
    }
}
```

### Frontend (HTML/CSS/JS)

#### Opción 1: Hosting Estático (Netlify/Vercel)

```bash
# netlify.toml
[build]
  publish = "."
  command = "echo 'No build required'"

[[redirects]]
  from = "/api/*"
  to = "https://api.ionik.com/:splat"
  status = 200
```

#### Opción 2: Servidor Propio

```nginx
# /etc/nginx/sites-available/ionik-web
server {
    listen 80;
    server_name ionik.com www.ionik.com;
    root /var/www/ionik;
    index index.html;
    
    location / {
        try_files $uri $uri/ =404;
    }
    
    location /api/ {
        proxy_pass http://localhost:3000/;
    }
}
```

